.TH ARGOS-VIEWER 1 "November 2026" "Argos 0.1.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
argos-viewer \- simple and fast photo viewer for GNOME (Argos)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B argos-viewer
[\fIFILE\fR|\fIFOLDER\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Argos shows the photos of a folder as a grid of thumbnails, with a folder tree
on the side, and opens them in a viewer with a thumbnail strip, a status bar and
a properties panel. The mouse wheel goes to the next or previous photo,
Ctrl + wheel zooms around the pointer, a double click shows the photo full
screen. Photos can be rotated, cropped and saved in another format.
.PP
With a photo, Argos opens its folder and shows the photo; with a folder, the
grid of that folder; without argument, the last folder opened (or Pictures).
If Argos is already running, the request goes to the running instance.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/argos/settings.json
Preferences.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/thumbnails/
Thumbnails, shared with Nautilus and other file managers.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/argos/undo/
Originals kept for "Undo" after saving an edited photo (removed after a day).
.SH AUTHOR
Tof
